# Server-only key used for keyed (HMAC) hashing of low-entropy values at
# rest — currently just Session.ipHash (a plain hash of an IP address
# would be trivially reversible; IPv4 space is only ~4 billion values).
#
# Copy this file to app_secret.txt (gitignored) and fill in a real
# random value. Generate one with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
#
# Rotating this value invalidates nothing stored (ipHash is advisory,
# not a security boundary) but means old ipHash values can no longer be
# recomputed/matched against a fresh one.
change-me-to-a-long-random-value
